and being a conservative on the south  side of chicago  is not  an easy thing to do  especially when you are  a black  pastor  preacher in the community  [Music]  can you believe it i'm still here that's  right living inside this tent from  november 20th to february 28th bringing  to you the awareness that you need to  know about the violence in chicago but  also to raise as much money as we  possibly can to build a center here on  this block that is much needed called oh  block it's called oh block because it's  named after a young man who was shot and  killed the gangs took the o in his name  after od perry  and begin to call it o block well we  decided we're going to keep the o but  we're going to change it to opportunity  block i want to thank fox for giving me  the opportunity every single day to  bring to you rooftop revelations where i  share with you my viewpoints thoughts  and opinions as it relates to what's  going on in chicago but also around our  great country  i get a lot of text messages and emails  and questions  surrounding  a question that has  come at me so many times  and the question is  how did you become a conservative  [Music]  and i always tell the same story how i  was at ball state university majoring in  political science and i never will  forget  it was a political science 101 class my  first political science class  where the professor put a bunch of  viewpoints on the on the board  on one side he had  views of conservatives on one side he  had views of liberals but you didn't  know that because he had them covered up  and they were switched  the conservative views were on the right  the i mean the liberal views were on the  right and the conservative reviews were  on the left  but we didn't know that because they  were covered  and he began to go down the list  and he said circle the ones or write the  ones that you agree with  and after going through the list of  thoughts and views  he uncovered the words  and there they were conservative  liberal  and when i looked at it i discovered  that  for the first time i understood that my  views were more more aligned to being a  conservative  but then the professor went on after  little dialogue and discussion of the  views and he said  if you are conservative  and you hold these viewpoints it is most  likely  that you align with the republican party  whoa  if you hold these viewpoints is more  likely  the liberal viewpoints you're aligned  with the democratic party  and for the first time ever  i was challenged  with being a democrat  because after all i had been taught all  of my life and i had seen it in my home  and  that that blacks are democrats and  that's just the way that it is  but after looking at that board and  staring it set me on a path  to try and discover  what i really believe  not what  they were forcing upon me or not what  they were trying to demand for me to  believe  but what  at my core in my heart  what did i really believe  and i discovered  after four years of  college at ball state university  where i got a degree in political  science  i discovered  i'm conservative  but that discovery let me tell you  has come with a lot of heartache and a  lot of pain  because see  here i am years later  on the south side of chicago  and being a conservative on the south  side of chicago  is not  an easy thing to do  especially when you are a black  pastor  preacher  in the community  i could tell you on and on about so many  things  that have happened to me just because  i've declared  i'm a conservative  just because i said i vote  republican  you wouldn't believe it but let me tell  you  i've been  threatened so many times  do you know that  the union's even picketed my church and  my house where i live  do you know that there was a governor  that i endorsed  uh he eventually won the republican  governor bruce rauner  and when i endorsed him do you know that  my family  was threatened so much that  they had to move us  to a place  just to hide  to protect my family  because of all the death threats  [Music]  being a conservative  [Music]  has had a great price  [Music]  do you not know that  because i decided to say i'm a  conservative and i'm a republican  and i'm not going to budge on it  i lost  three-fourths of my congregation  i lost three-fourths of our budget  just because i said i'm going to  be conservative  that i hold conservative values  but here's a heartbreaking thing  do you not know that most blacks  hold conservative values  [Music]  but we have been so indoctrinated  to believe that we most  that we must  vote democrat there is no other way  [Music]  i'm hoping and praying  that  my example of being steadfast  [Music]  and showing people that you can  be different  that you don't have to abide by the  status quo  i'm praying that it will show people  that you can stand on what you believe  so  here i am on this rooftop  a conservative  black preacher  on the south side of chicago  trying to do the very best that i can  possibly do  for the people in our community  for the people in chicago  and for our great country  and for that  i don't believe i have anything to be  ashamed of  as i always say god bless you  god bless america  and thank you for tuning in to rooftop  revelations  until tomorrow  peace  you
 

